<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!--
    Merged into the bundle's Info.plist by tauri-bundler.

    Local network access. Since macOS 15 an app must say why it talks to the
    local network, and from 26 a GUI-launched app without this key is denied
    LAN traffic silently: no error, no prompt, and every camera looks absent.
    It never shows in development, because a process started from Terminal
    inherits Terminal's own permission.

    The string is shown verbatim in the macOS permission prompt.

    Verify after a build with:
      plutil -p Meerkat.app/Contents/Info.plist | grep NSLocalNetwork
  -->
  <key>NSLocalNetworkUsageDescription</key>
  <string>Meerkat looks for PTZ cameras on your local network with each brand's own discovery broadcast, and changes a camera's address or opens its web page only when you ask it to.</string>
</dict>
</plist>
